                <pb facs="0608" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10470: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-03T15:00:00+08:00">June 3, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 3—10:48 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Cantonese naval forces occupied Wuchow last night without opposition. River will
                    be reopened to navigation immediately.</p>
                <p>Legation has been informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
